## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

**Planes:** front petal polish; living wet ginger; suspended neroli/violet silk; rear golden cedar/root; through-line petitgrain fiber; outward Romandolide aura.

| Window | Intended event | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| opening, 0-5 min | bitter rind and green twig expose wet ginger | NOT TESTED |
| top, 5-30 min | ginger contracts as neroli silk expands | NOT TESTED |
| heart, 30-120 min | violet cloth catches orange-petal light | NOT TESTED |
| late heart, 2-6 h | green stem dries into cedar/vetiver grain | NOT TESTED |
| drydown, 6-24 h | hayed sandal release sits within one clean-woody aura | NOT TESTED |

**Nineteen textures:** luminous; waxed; bitter; wet-cut; crisp; fatty; fibrous; petal-silk; tailored-cloth; leafy; stem-dry; humid; mineral; pencil-dry; rooty; hayed; sheer; slow; clean-woody.

**Ten links:** bergamot→petitgrain; petitgrain→ginger; ginger→jasmine tissue; tissue→neroli; neroli→violet cloth; cloth→green stem; stem→cedar; cedar→vetiver; vetiver→tonka-sandal; base→Romandolide. Pressure comes from bitter rind, ginger cut, green stem and dry grain; release comes from neroli silk, Hedione space, Sandalore and the slow matrix. Petitgrain's woody-green fiber recurs from aperture to cedar; ginger dryness recurs through vetiver and Koavone. All are intended hypotheses.

## Source-lineage conservation ledger

The immutable V5 floor is 58 ideal rows, ten modules, five windows, ten links, nineteen textures, and one exact musk. This successor preserves those counts while re-authoring their relations. The complete machine-readable row and module dispositions above are binding. `KEEP/REBASE` retains a target-linked function; `IDEAL-ONLY` preserves an inventory-independent hypothesis; every rejection names an isolated return test. No current-stock absence compresses the ideal.

