## Candidate-survival and omission audit

Every current row owns one audible or structural function; quiet Benzyl Benzoate is disclosed as mass, not complexity. Neroli is central through a five-owner flower architecture rather than ingredient representation alone. No Calone, Dihydromyrcenol, Floralozone, dense resin, vanilla, cinnamon, tobacco, or multi-musk block is admitted. **Opus V structural overlap** is `10 shared rows / 0.393333 candidate raw share / 0.208333 donor coverage`: the raw share exceeds 0.35, but the unchanged conjunctive gate does not form a cluster below 12 shared rows. This governance PASS is not sensory independence and remains a review caution.

Highest-value omission is the petal-body block: Aurantiol 150 + Oranger Crystals 10% DPG 110 + Farnesol 20 versus a defined 280 uL DPG replacement in the omission concentrate, while leaving the protected bergamot/petitgrain/neroli/ginger nucleus unchanged. Add 181 uL DPG outside the main concentrate before final ethanol adjustment so both completed samples carry the same DPG total; the comparison remains a whole-block intervention, not a single-material proof. A null result tests only this dose and protocol.

